      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The key observations:\n- Unused fields: `bufReader0`, `STRING_END_NO_EOL`, `STRING_END_EOL` are declared but never used in this test\n- The test verifies that a `BoundedReader` (limit=3) wrapped in a `BufferedReader` doesn't hang when `readLine()` is called twice (once reads up to the bound, once hits EOF)\n- No explanation of WHY two `readLine()` calls are needed or what outcome is expected\n\nI'll write an improved version with cleaner scope and a brief intent comment.The improved test compiles successfully. The changes made were: removed three unused fields (`bufReader0`, `STRING_END_NO_EOL`, `STRING_END_EOL`) and unused imports, renamed `bufReader1` to `sourceReader` for clarity, renamed the local variable `mr` to `boundedReader`, and added a one-line comment explaining why two `readLine()` calls are needed — all without altering the runtime behaviour."
